From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshijiang <ssj1595329871@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3566-lckfb-tspi: enable eMMC HS200

The Taishan Pi eMMC must run in HS200 mode. On RK356x SoCs the MMC DDR52
mode produces corrupt writes with some eMMC devices; only HS200 is
reliable. This mirrors the change upstream Home Assistant made for the
Home Assistant Green board, which runs the same RK3566 SoC:

  green: emmc use HS200 mode
    &sdhci { mmc-hs200-1_8v; }

Without this the data partition can be silently corrupted while Home
Assistant is writing its state, which is especially painful on the 1 GB
variants where the eMMC is also small.

Signed-off-by: sunshijiang <ssj1595329871@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-lckfb-tspi.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-lckfb-tspi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-lckfb-tspi.dts
index 4e0c4a1b2f3..7a1d9c5e6b8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-lckfb-tspi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-lckfb-tspi.dts
@@ -570,6 +570,7 @@
 &sdhci {
 	bus-width = <8>;
+	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
 	max-frequency = <200000000>;
 	non-removable;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&emmc_bus8 &emmc_clk &emmc_cmd &emmc_datastrobe &emmc_rstnout>;
